{
  "description": "Touchque Login user-store requests (user_store.verify_password, user_store.get_user, user_store.ping) exactly as the backend sends them: made by running the authenticator backend's own code (how it asks your user store, and its webhook signing: stableStringify() and hmacHex()) with the API secret \"test_secret\" and recording each POST. Per vector: body = the exact JSON text POSTed (UTF-8); x_signature = its x-signature header (the body's signature field holds the same value); secret = the API secret to verify with; valid = whether verification must pass; canonical = what a verifier builds from body (for a valid vector, the exact string Touchque signed): the members without signature, top-level keys sorted, each written as JSON.stringify writes it (an unpaired surrogate as a lowercase \\udxxx escape; U+2028, U+2029, <>& and non-ASCII raw), and hex HMAC-SHA256(secret, UTF-8 of canonical) equals x_signature exactly when valid; expected_payload = what verify must hand back: every body member, signature included, with each unpaired surrogate replaced by U+FFFD (null when valid is false). Timestamps are fixed in the past, so verify with the freshness check off (tolerance 0); every jti is unique. The file is ASCII: a non-ASCII character is a \\u escape of this JSON file, so body and canonical hold it raw.",
  "source": "Generated by the authenticator backend (its user store requests and webhook signing: stableStringify, hmacHex).",
